    <node id="&quot;KEVIN LEWIS (FOOTBALLER, BORN 1940)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kevin Lewis (footballer, born 1940) is an English former professional footballer who played as a winger for Sheffield United, Liverpool, and Huddersfield Town. He also played for Wigan Athletic in the Cheshire League, scoring three goals in eight games. Currently he is a pub landlord in the Staffordshire moorlands."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kevin Lewis (footballer, born 1940) is an English former professional footballer who played as a winger for Sheffield United, Liverpool, and Huddersfield Town."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0386-c6820b88dce0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEVIN LEWIS (FOOTBALLER, BORN 1952)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kevin William Lewis (footballer, born 1952) is an English former footballer who played in the Football League for Crewe Alexandra and Stoke City. His nephew of the same name was also a footballer who played for Stoke City. Lewis was born in Hull and played in the youth teams of Manchester United before joining Stoke City in 1972. He never was really able to force his way into Tony Waddington's side and after 16 appearances in four seasons he left the Victoria Ground. He spent three years out of the game before joining Crewe."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0386-c6820b88dce0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEVIN LEWIS (FOOTBALLER, BORN 1970)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kevin Lewis (footballer, born 1970) is an English former footballer who played in the Football League for Stoke City. His uncle of the same name, was also a footballer who played for Stoke City. Lewis was born in Kingston upon Hull and played in the youth team of Stoke City. With Stoke's 1987–88 campaign coming to a close with nothing to play for manager Mick Mills decided to give youth team players some first team experience and Lewis made his a substitute in a 2–0 defeat away at Millwall on 30 April 1988. He"</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0386-c6820b88dce0</data>
    </node>
